updated_at: "2026-11-12T12:50:47.924Z"
author: codex-github230-1111
comments[66]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-11T10:19:28.756Z",codex-github230-1111,"Read issue 230 and all comments. Branch starts from main; PR229 changes workflows and docs separately. Plan: distinguish explicit importer identity from references, preserve curated linked content, retain legacy persisted provenance, and prove behavior with real SDK trackers and behavioral reverts. Task-specific gate budget applies: focused importer/sync/dependent tests, lint and typecheck; full suite only within 45 minutes."
  "2026-11-11T10:24:30.654Z",codex-github230-1111,"Implemented separate durable import identity lookup; shared gh references no longer select owners or collide. Curated links merge provenance/lifecycle while deterministic importer records mirror content. New real SDK regressions pass 9/9, including no-git curated links and byte-identical legacy resync beside shared references. Reviewing existing tests that assumed tag-only ownership; updating mirror fixtures to explicit importer identities."
  "2026-11-11T10:33:45.352Z",codex-github230-1111,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable package copy: rebuilt after restoring released matchImportedIssue, prepareGithubImport and verifyImportIdempotency plus tag-only identity lookup. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/reference-import-identity.test.ts: 14 tests, 13 fail, 1 pass. All four required scenarios fail: single curated Chore, shared references, mirror title refresh beside a reference, and byte-identical legacy resync beside a reference. The passing legacy link-marker case is existing supported behavior. Package worktree was never reverted. Fixed regressions are being rerun through pm test; full npm test follows within the task budget."
  "2026-11-11T10:39:30.901Z",codex-github230-1111,"Linked pm test run passed 16/16 (real SDK trackers, both import modes, no-git linking, legacy compatibility, safe PR conflict rendering and dependency routing). Lint and typecheck pass; docstring gate documents 29 files/280 declarations; duplication gate has zero clones at the unchanged 50-token threshold across 30 authored modules. Added seeded preview/apply equivalence coverage. Full npm test is running with two workers and a 45-minute cap; npm/bun release:check and coverage are delegated to CI under the explicit task gate budget."
  "2026-11-11T10:55:16.026Z",codex-github230-1111,"Optional full npm test was stopped under the task gate budget: an unrelated closeout workflow file had already used over 11 minutes before its large decision matrix. No failures were reported in the observed output before cancellation; this is incomplete evidence, not a passing full suite. Running all 46 required importer/sync/direct-dependent and sync-workflow test files separately now, with two file workers and a hard 1200-second limit per file. CI owns full-suite and release certification."
  "2026-11-11T11:09:29.505Z",codex-github230-1111,The audit also found a separate Projects v2 board-import reference fallback. Tracked static evidence and required real-SDK reproduction in pm-github-project-reference-followup; board ownership/mirroring is a separate model from the gated REST issue importer and was not changed here.
  "2026-11-11T11:38:48.163Z",codex-github230-1111,"Final fixture reruns passed: import-fidelity 53 pass/1 existing SDK quarantine; handler failures 38/38; import projection 6/6; label-model properties 3/3 (including both 500-case SDK corpora); daily-sync properties 3/3. The new regression files pass 18/18, including mixed-case legacy URLs. Corrected an embedded child-script fixture import and verified coverage-remainder 25/25; repeating its final file with explicit pinned-CLI PATH. Standalone new regressions now pin their child CLI too."
  "2026-11-11T11:42:48.057Z",codex-github230-1111,"Final local evidence: 46 selected files attempted with two workers and a 1200-second limit per file. Completed 45 files: 869 tests, 867 pass, zero fail, two unchanged SDK quarantines. import-gate.test.ts reached its 20-minute cap after 63 passes and one canceled test; it is incomplete CI evidence. Every other file passed after fixture corrections. Exact file command was node --test --test-concurrency=1 followed by that file, with the repository CLI first on PATH and global Git configuration disabled. The linked regression command was rerun through pm test --run --progress after the disposable behavioral revert: 18/18 pass. Latest revert: 17 tests, 16 fail, one legacy link-marker pass; all four required scenarios fail. Lint, typecheck, test compilation, 280 documented declarations and zero duplication at the unchanged threshold pass. Full npm test, coverage and npm/Bun release certification remain for CI. No consumer holds or trackers were changed."
  "2026-11-11T11:47:33.244Z",codex-github230-1111,"PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233 . Code commit e9e0c9a. The claim is released and this item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification. Final privacy scan passed across 9334 Git objects with approved identities and no secret or host-path findings; tracker diff gate passed. Strict health passed with isolated global extension discovery; ambient discovery had an SDK version skew, while integrity/history remained valid. Full-suite, timed-out import-gate completion, coverage and npm/Bun release checks remain for CI. Projects v2 board fallback remains separately tracked in pm-github-project-reference-followup."
  "2026-11-11T14:06:28.712Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 2 resumes from ed050d3 with a clean worktree. Read all four unresolved threads and the complete latest CodeRabbit review body, including its outside-diff upstream-target finding and scope-check note. Plan: synchronize all non-content side data for curated links; reject contradictory explicit identities before writes with normalized compatibility; persist/replay atomic import plans through retries; and guard outbound status/export targets. Keep review threads open for the orchestrator. Existing Projects follow-up audit records remain append-only as required by the task rules."
  "2026-11-11T14:23:38.805Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 2 side-data inventory: after a content merge, the mirror path applies native lifecycle transitions, synchronizes GitHub comments as annotations, persists github_* source dates/state/closure provenance, reports counts, links dependencies, and runs provenance/privacy gates. Curated updates now perform the same non-content steps. Body-only fetched comments route to annotations for curated items. SDK transaction contract uses payload-bound ordered steps: recovery replays the recorded original entries, mutations, targets, comments and dependency inputs before polling new GitHub data; a later normal sync observes changed input. Identity validation shares one normalized explicit-identity path across import, refresh, sync and export; contradictory values refuse before writes. Outbound sync/export now ignore shared references by default and offer explicit historical tag-only opt-in with competing-owner refusal."
  "2026-11-11T14:34:18.885Z",codex-github230-1111,"Review regression baseline: 21 real-SDK cases passed across curated side data, explicit-identity refusal and spelling compatibility, six original-plan crash boundaries, upstream plan conflicts and actual sync/export HTTP writes. Added a further dependency replay case for an unchanged item in a mixed batch: record the complete original dependency input, interrupt, change the remote body, then recover the original edge. Replacing the prior fake incomplete-compensation test with a real SDK transaction also checks that compensation recovery reuses the saved plan. Broad gates cover 49 affected/import/refresh/identity/sync files, two workers, each invocation capped at 20 minutes; import-gate is partitioned by exhaustive disjoint test-name prefixes."
  "2026-11-11T15:09:38.145Z",codex-github230-1111,"Final review regression run through pm test --run --progress passed 29/29 cases, including generated preview/apply agreement. Import-gate completed 73/73 cases across four alphabetic name partitions; all 56 declaration prefixes were checked for coverage by those partitions. A redundant non-letter pattern matched the Node file wrapper, was stopped, removed from linked tests and excluded from counts. The closeout workflow matrix reached its 20-minute cap after 143 passing cases with no assertion failures. Real compensation testing follows the public SDK contract: delete compensation retains history and reserves the original ID. Recovery now keeps the plan and returns github_import_plan_drift instead of applying changed input; explicit SDK restore of the original birth version then permits the exact saved plan to finish. The atomic file passed 11/11 including this refusal-and-restore case. Read-only identity exploration still exposes contradictory stored claims, while write planners refuse them."
  "2026-11-11T15:10:46.699Z",codex-github230-1111,"Behavioral revert proof, executed only in a disposable package copy with real temp SDK trackers: restoring round-one prepareGithubImport/runImport causes 4 of 6 curated side-data cases to fail (2 atomic annotation compatibility controls pass); restoring importIdentityKeys/matchImportedIssue causes all 7 explicit identity refusal/normalization cases to fail; restoring runImport and disabling persisted-plan dispatch in importGithubAtomic causes all 12 crash/dependency/missing-plan cases to fail; restoring planSync/buildExportPlan causes all 3 upstream planning, wire-write and generated preview/apply cases to fail. The same atomic replay revert makes the real incomplete-compensation/explicit-restore test fail (1/1). Every mutation was restored in a finally block; the fixed package copy is running the full review regression file again. Review thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62J6R5 and PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62KLhP use curated side-data tests; PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62KLhK uses explicit identity cases; PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62KLhO uses original-plan replay plus compensation. Latest CodeRabbit outside-diff upstream comment uses the three upstream cases. No review thread was replied to, resolved or reacted to."
  "2026-11-11T15:17:36.076Z",codex-github230-1111,"Final round-2 evidence: fixed disposable source copy matches the package code byte-for-byte and passes 30/30 review regressions after restoration. An additional mutation-payload drift test fails 1/1 when only commitGithubImportTransaction is restored to round one; fixed code returns github_import_plan_drift before native writes and succeeds once the original saved plan is restored. Final unique completed gates cover 48 files (51 bounded invocations): 1121 tests, 1119 pass, 0 fail, 2 existing pm-cli#1656 quarantines. Import-gate is complete at 73/73; closeout-workflow is the sole capped file, 143 passes then 1 cancellation at 20 minutes. Fresh atomic gate is 11/11, refresh 34 pass plus 1 existing quarantine, import fidelity 53 pass plus 1 existing quarantine; packed npm/native Bun import projection is 6/6. Lint, typecheck, builds, docstrings and strict health with isolated global discovery pass. Full npm/Bun release and exact 100-percent coverage remain for CI under the requested gate budget; prior head CI reported 99.94-percent branch coverage, which is not certification for this change. Counts exclude the stopped redundant regex run and superseded failures fixed in compatibility fixtures. CI handoff: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233/checks . Original Projects follow-up remains open because task rules require out-of-scope tracking and append-only audit records. No Projects code changed in round two. The main item stays in_progress; releasing only this agent claim before commit and push."
  "2026-11-11T16:08:01.288Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 3 starts from clean head 080f1e6; round-2 work is accepted. Read the three orchestrator findings in full. Plan: replace package-wide GitHub issue URL parsing with one URL/path-segment helper; persist and enforce privacy preflight verdicts before recovery writes; and allow legacy number-only promotion only for one implied repository, reporting ambiguous legacy references as typed summary conflicts. Preserve accepted side-data and original-plan recovery behavior, add real SDK tracker regressions and disposable behavioral reverts, run bounded affected-file gates, then release the claim and push."
  "2026-11-11T16:22:16.093Z",codex-github230-1111,"Read the current GitHub review snapshot: 7 threads, 7 complete comments/diffs with no further comment pages, and 4 review bodies. Three newer threads include the rejected-recovery finding, retained committed refresh work (PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62PHLJ), and CodeQL polynomial URL-related parsing (PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62PrYX). The shared URL parser removes path replacement and whole-path issue/PR regex parsing; repository suffix normalization now uses a linear scan. Recovery now saves privacy verdicts and requires both a saved pass and a fresh pass before replay, including refresh. Retained committed plans are discovered before refresh polls new data, closing the related side-data replay class. Initial round-3 focused suite passed 26/26 real-SDK cases, including reserved repository/owner names, decorated URLs, legacy ambiguity, and failed/missing/forged privacy preflights with unchanged documents and histories."
  "2026-11-11T16:55:04.657Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 3: all GitHub issue/PR identity paths now share URL and fixed-segment parsing. Ambiguous number-only legacy provenance is a mention with typed ambiguous_legacy_github_identity summary evidence; a single repository or explicit repository still resolves. Every replay requires a saved passing preflight plus a fresh scan before mutation. Also fixed retained committed refresh side-data discovery (Greptile PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62PHLJ) and replaced the slash-suffix regex flagged by CodeQL alert 12 with linear trimming. Lint, typecheck, docstrings (30 files, 276 declarations), and duplication (zero authored duplicated lines) pass. Broad dependent-file gates remain running with two workers and 20-minute invocation caps; closeout-workflow reached its cap and needs CI certification."
  "2026-11-11T17:04:52.430Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 3 read receipt: all 3 supplied blocking findings, 7 review threads with 7 complete comments/proposed diffs, and 4 complete review bodies were read (no remaining pages), plus the full CodeQL alert 12 payload. Accepted round-2 fixes remain intact. The shared URL parser is used by import identity, refresh, sync/export ownership, diagnostics, blockers, closeout, discussions and Projects URL inputs; transport pagination/origin checks remain transport-only. Repository normalization preserves released opaque keys while removing the quadratic suffix regex. Strict pm health passes with two advisory warnings. Full npm/Bun release and 100% coverage certification remain CI work under the explicit gate budget."
  "2026-11-11T17:16:29.057Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 3 behavioral revert proof (real SDK trackers in a disposable package copy): restoring only explicitGithubKey to 080f1e6 produces 6 failures and 12 compatibility passes in the URL segments cases; bypassing assertGithubImportReplayPreflight produces 3 privacy/no-write failures; restoring only importIdentityKeys and matchImportedIssue produces 1 ambiguous-legacy failure with 2 compatibility controls passing. Restoring runRefresh produces 2 retained-annotation recovery failures. Replacing normalizeGithubRepository with the released suffix regex produces 1 bounded adversarial-input failure; reverting only the workflow conflict projection produces 1 formatter failure. Commands: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern <case-prefix> test/review-round3-identity.test.ts (prefixes: URL segments, recovery preflight, number-only legacy, refresh recovers, repository normalization), plus the sync PR includes pattern in test/import-conflict-report.test.ts. The fixed implementation was restored in finally; both files pass 30/30, and 11 implementation/test/workflow files match the package source byte-for-byte. All four importer-gate partitions pass: 16+6+33+18 = 73 cases."
  "2026-11-11T17:19:33.716Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 3 final local gates: 51 completed affected/required files across 54 bounded invocations, 1189 passing tests, zero failures, two existing pm-cli#1656 skips. This includes all 73 importer-gate cases, refresh 34 passes plus one skip, identity 20, cited adoption 46, atomic 11, quarantine guard 2, accepted review regressions 30 and new round-3 regressions 29. Initial compatibility failures were fixed and their complete files rerun successfully. The linked pm test run passes 29/29; restored disposable proof files pass 30/30 separately. closeout-workflow reached its 20-minute cap after 62 passes and one canceled case, without assertion failures; CI must finish it. Build, lint, typecheck, docstrings, duplication, strict tracker health and privacy audit pass. Full npm/Bun release checks and exact 100% coverage remain uncertified locally under the explicit budget. No outstanding implementation blocker or new follow-up was found; the existing Projects v2 follow-up remains open. Releasing only this author claim and leaving the issue in progress."
  "2026-11-11T18:13:07.803Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 4 plan: SDK declaration audit found public writeFileAtomic(targetPath, contents, {createParentDirectories?}) in sdk/index.d.ts and core/fs/fs-utils.d.ts. Use that helper for same-directory staging, fsync the completed candidate, publish by rename (replacement) or atomic no-replace link (plans and leases), then fsync directories. Audit found recovery plans, comment-sync leases, breaker-election markers, and webhook delivery/cursor/completion state. SDK-owned native history and transaction journals remain SDK-managed; scripts only emit derived output or disposable test mutations. Corrupt/unreadable plan contents will receive github_import_plan_corrupt with explicit restore/journal reconciliation steps; only ENOENT means missing. Add real SDK tracker regressions for native partial-write faults, crash before publication, concurrent readers, and clean zero-item retries. Round-3 implementation is accepted and retained."
  "2026-11-11T18:20:22.259Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 4 review read receipt: 13 threads with 13 comments/diffs and 6 review bodies enumerated without remaining pages; all 6 new thread texts/diffs and the new CodeRabbit body read, carrying forward the 7 already accepted round-3 threads. Q98c and Q98i are already fixed by 90d530f; Q984 is marked addressed there. New unrelated minor findings are tracked in pm-github-curated-reopen-followup, pm-github-pr-url-alias-followup and pm-github-blocker-format-followup after searching existing items. The outside-diff README owner-linking instructions now use github_url. Retain required append-only tracking evidence despite the bot scope suggestion to delete the existing Projects follow-up. Round-4 code remains scoped to durable publication and typed corrupt-plan recovery."
  "2026-11-11T18:37:25.732Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 4 focused expanded corpus passes 11/11 on real non-git SDK trackers. Native faults write actual partial bytes only to hidden candidates; empty-source retry and subsequent real import still work. SIGKILL at the flushed-candidate hook leaves zero native items and no discoverable final plan. Concurrent readers observe previous complete state during publication, failure and interruption; retry succeeds. Empty, unparseable and structurally incomplete JSON all produce github_import_plan_corrupt with restore/journal recovery instructions. The same validateGithubImportPlan function checks both reads and apply. Build, lint, typecheck, docstrings (31 files, 277 declarations), zero-duplication gate and strict health pass. The initial privacy audit passes 9459 objects; final commit will be audited again. Bounded dependent-file gates are running without failures so far."
  "2026-11-11T18:42:15.474Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 4 bounded sweep found one compatibility edge: an existing comment lease in a read-only directory must report contention rather than degrade because staging cannot write there. Added an early lstat existence hint, retaining the final exclusive hard link as the authoritative race check. The full import-lock file will be rerun after the remaining sweep; the real permission test and cross-process contention tests cover the preserved contract. No SDK or dependency change was needed."
  "2026-11-11T19:05:49.794Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 4 behavioral revert proof in a disposable package copy, using real SDK trackers and only native filesystem fault injection: old persistGithubImportPlan behavior (retaining the observation hook) gives 2 failures: partial final JSON poisons an empty-source retry, and SIGKILL exposes a final plan before publication. Old readGithubImportPlan gives 6 missing typed-corruption refusals. Replacing writeGithubStateAtomic with the prior direct-write behavior gives 3 concurrent-reader failures (publication, write failure, interruption). Old acquireImportLock gives 1 observed empty reserved lease. Revert commands use node --test --test-concurrency=1 with the matching partial native plan/crash after plan, corrupt recovery plan, concurrent state readers, and failed atomic lock publication name patterns. Total: 12 expected failures, no cancellations. Restored fixed code passes the complete durable-recovery file 11/11 plus the lease regression 1/1; all 9 code/docs/test files match the package implementation byte-for-byte. The package worktree was never mutated by these reverts."
  "2026-11-11T19:16:39.154Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 4 final portable regression proof: the initial Node-only filesystem replacement harness did not inject faults under Bun, so fault injection now uses the explicit prepublication hook with real partial candidate writes and injected EIO. No pm SDK or filesystem APIs are mocked in the new durable-recovery corpus. Node and native Bun each pass 11/11, and the lease regression passes under Bun. Repeated behavioral reverts preserve the observation hooks while restoring unsafe direct writer/lease behavior: plan writer 2 failures, old reader 6, direct state publisher 3, direct lease publisher 1. All are behavioral failures (poisoned zero-source retry, premature final publication, absent corruption refusal, or partial bytes observed). Restored source passes 11 durable cases plus 1 lease case and matches all 9 package code/docs/test files byte-for-byte."
  "2026-11-11T19:16:39.997Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 4 final gates: 51 completed files / 54 bounded invocations, 1161 passes, zero failures, two existing pm-cli#1656 skips. All 73 importer-gate cases pass; full import-lock recheck passes 25/25 after preserving read-only contention. Refresh is 34 passes plus one existing skip; accepted review files pass 30/30 and 29/29. Linked pm runs of node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/durable-recovery.test.ts and bun test --timeout 60000 test/durable-recovery.test.ts each pass 11/11. Automatic test-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so these outcomes and revert evidence are recorded in comments. closeout-workflow reached its 20-minute cap after 65 passes and one cancellation without assertion failures. Full npm/Bun release and exact 100% coverage remain CI certification at the linked PR checks page. Six logical writes now use four shared atomic-publication entry points; SDK-owned native journals/history remain SDK-managed. No new SDK gap or dependency change. Three minor review follow-ups remain open. Releasing this author claim and leaving the main issue in progress."
  "2026-11-11T20:13:15.527Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 5: claimed the main item and the two existing follow-ups now in scope, without creating duplicates. Keep structured URL identity parsing strict. Prose extraction tracks balanced brackets, matching emphasis and trailing punctuation. Every unsupported HTTP URL becomes a visible unparsed_url reference, never a guessed hash from its interior, so it cannot make an item cleared or produce a cleared comment. Explicit URL alias resolution is shared by ownership and refresh, retaining the parsed issue/PR kind. New real non-git SDK tracker tests cover all requested wrappers, punctuation, the exact mixed-reference reproduction, unsupported URLs and case/underscore aliases. Review snapshot: 21 threads/comments and 9 reviews enumerated without further pages; the two targeted full texts/diffs were read (SJvl and Q99D). Accepted round-4 changes remain intact."
  "2026-11-11T20:30:23.327Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 5 false-clear path audit also found self-exclusion treated every gh: tag as ownership. collectBlockerReferences now uses the same authoritative importIdentityKeys resolver to exclude only actual self identity, retaining reference-tagged blockers. Added a real tracker reproduction with gh:o/r#2 plus the mixed closed/open Markdown links; it must retain open #2. Legacy generated owner markers still resolve through the existing compatibility rule. No other ownership or content merge behavior changed. The focused file now contains 31 cases; behavioral reverts will cover the collector independently."
  "2026-11-11T21:06:54.225Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 5 final behavioral revert proof in a disposable package copy with real SDK trackers and real HTTP transport: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern PATTERN test/github-url.test.ts. Restoring only the previous tokenizer body (retaining span metadata) makes all 17 ^Markdown cases fail; restoring parseBlockerReferences makes all 8 ^Unparsed cases fail; restoring collectBlockerReferences makes the ^Reference tags case fail; restoring selectRefreshTargets makes all 5 ^Refresh excludes PRs cases fail. Total 31 expected behavioral failures, zero cancellations. Each required wrapper and punctuation case fails on revert, including the supplied mixed closed/open URL reproduction. The restored implementation passes 31/31 and all seven code/docs/test files match the package implementation byte-for-byte. The package worktree was never reverted."
  "2026-11-11T21:06:55.106Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 5 final gates: 54 selected test files / 57 bounded invocations, 56 completed invocations, 1231 passes, zero assertion failures, 2 existing pm-cli#1656 skips. All 73 import-gate cases pass across four disjoint name partitions. closeout-workflow reached its 20-minute cap after 69 passes and one cancellation; it remains incomplete CI evidence. Final blockers recheck passes 35/35. Linked pm runs of node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/github-url.test.ts and bun test --timeout 60000 test/github-url.test.ts each pass 31/31; follow-up pm runs pass 26 blocker cases and 5 alias cases. Project policy disables automatic test-result writes, so exact outcomes are recorded here. Lint, typecheck, build, test compilation, docstrings (31 files / 278 declarations), zero duplication and strict tracker health pass (two existing advisories). Full npm/Bun release and exact 100% coverage remain CI certification under the task budget. Read receipt: two supplied findings; 21 threads / 21 comments and 9 reviews enumerated without remaining pages, with the two targeted full texts/diffs read (PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62SJvl and PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62Q99D). The accepted rounds remain intact. Releasing all three scoped claims; items remain in progress. Curated reopen and Projects follow-ups remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-11T22:07:06.775Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 6: accepted head rechecked clean. Audit every existing-item write target against exactly one authoritative GitHub owner, including deterministic upsert collisions, URL/alias matches, refresh, closeout and durable replay/finalization. Choose a typed collision refusal rather than silently reassigning an existing deterministic ID; preserve byte-identical item content on refusal and ordinary owner-matching idempotency. Real SDK tracker matrix and isolated behavioral reverts will cover each path. The completion-date reopen defect remains deferred. Current review receipt: one supplied blocking finding; 21 threads/comments and 10 reviews enumerated without further pages. The curated-reopen thread and latest CodeRabbit body were read in full."
  "2026-11-11T22:21:13.228Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 6 implementation: typed github_import_owner_conflict refuses occupied deterministic IDs rather than allocating suffixes. One shared positive owner assertion protects preflight and every SDK item-lock write, including replay, fidelity and annotations; bound delegates retain ambient mutation hooks. Plain CLI writes and dependency edges carry --expect-hash from the same live ownership read. URL-only, alias-only and number-only targets are checked independently. Closeout holds imported owners outside its delivery repository while retaining explicit native delivery for local items. Real SDK non-git matrix passes 21/21 under Node and Bun, including matching-owner idempotency and ambient hook controls. The bounded dependent sweep is now running with two workers."
  "2026-11-11T23:34:38.727Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 6 refinement: deterministic IDs, even alongside a matching reference tag, no longer confer ownership. Released source-number/link markers and generated source descriptions still resolve without migration; a real pre-fidelity marker control updates its original ID and then re-syncs byte-identically. Creation/content plans must retain the generated source marker before SDK updates, otherwise github_import_plan_ownership_invalid refuses before journal publication. Existing-item checks use live normalized ownership, locked SDK hooks, and CLI expected revisions. First-link provider/citation authorization is preserved without overriding explicit GitHub owners. Collision remedy restores intended provenance only for the intended item; otherwise select a different configured ID prefix or tracker and retain existing items/history. New relink fixtures use mutateItem and verify complete history chains plus the current item hash, rather than the birth-only import adapter. Both same-repository and cross-repository closeout transfers are held."
  "2026-11-11T23:48:50.034Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 6 final behavioral revert proof in disposable package copies only: disabling assertGithubImportOwner alone makes all 19 shared-guard cases fail; removing only ownedPmRun expected-hash arguments makes the real peer/CLI race fail with changed native body/history; disabling assertCloseoutGithubOwner makes both same-repository and cross-repository delivery cases fail. The source matrix has 22 refusal cases and four must-allow/ambient controls. The exact gated atomic upsert reproduction uses a valid URL-only transfer to other/project#8 and compares native item/history bytes before checking the refusal, so a late gate error cannot hide an overwrite. Curated collisions run without Git and include a matching reference tag, plus a second incoming issue to prove whole-batch refusal. Every relink verifies the full native history chain and its current item hash. Source revert commands are node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern PATTERN test/import-ownership.test.ts, with patterns ^Ownership (?!plain CLI|closeout|matching-owner|guard preserves), ^Ownership plain CLI, and ^Ownership closeout. Restored source passes 26/26. Rebuilding the artifact with only the owner assertion disabled makes the packed npm consumer regression fail; restoring and rebuilding makes that exact packed case pass 1/1. Its command is node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern \"^packed npm\" test/import-projection.test.ts. The packed case verifies the public CLI JSON github_import_owner_conflict code, both owner values and unchanged native bytes. All production code/docs and the relevant tests match their restored copies. No pm SDK mocks are used in the new matrix."
  "2026-11-11T23:48:51.488Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 6 final bounded gate receipt: 54 selected test files / 57 initial invocations, corrected with linked/full or targeted fixture rechecks; 53 completed files / 56 complete invocations contain 1220 tests: 1218 pass, zero remaining failures and two existing pm-cli#1656 skips. The importer gate passes all 73 cases in four disjoint partitions. closeout-workflow reached its 20-minute cap after 74 passes and one cancellation without an assertion failure; CI must certify that file and the full npm/Bun release/coverage gate. Both 500-case label models pass, as does their corrected shared-conversion case. Final linked pm runs of node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/import-ownership.test.ts and bun test --timeout 60000 test/import-ownership.test.ts each pass 26/26 with valid SDK mutation histories. Finalization, refresh, idempotency, SDK hooks, literal-field and packed consumer rechecks pass. Existing command-failure fixtures now seed real owners; deleted targets refuse at the SDK tombstone read before mutation and retain their history. Build, test compilation, lint, typecheck, docstrings (32 files / 287 declarations), zero duplication (33 authored modules) and strict tracker health pass with two existing advisories. No dependency or SDK pin changed; no new SDK gap or quarantine was introduced. Project policy disables automatic test-result records, so outcomes are recorded in comments. Current review receipt: one supplied blocking finding; 21 threads / 21 comments and 10 reviews enumerated without remaining pages. The curated-reopen thread PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62Q98t and the latest CodeRabbit body were read in full. Its completion-date reproduction is recorded on the deferred item without changing behavior. The two outside-diff read-path findings are tracked separately. CI evidence remains at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233/checks. Releasing this author claim; the main item remains in progress and follow-ups stay open or in progress."
  "2026-11-11T23:54:22.048Z",codex-github230-1111,"Final fixture tightening: the dependency-race regression now delegates listing to the real SDK and uses the real default ordering-cycle collector. The exact command node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern \"^Ownership dependency writes\" test/import-ownership.test.ts passes 1/1. In a disposable package copy, disabling only assertGithubImportOwner makes that same case fail 1/1; restoring it passes 1/1. Final test compilation and lint pass. This strengthens the existing 22-case behavioral revert proof without changing production code, test counts or the gate receipt. All tracker histories remain byte-prefix extensions of the accepted base and origin/main. Releasing only this author claim before commit; no item is closed."
  "2026-11-12T01:29:06.709Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 7 starts from accepted ownership head eeee95d. Merged current origin/main before new work. Read the supplied atomic dry-run review and all eight requested full thread bodies, AI-agent prompts and diffs. Plan: use a real initialized tracker for apply-equivalent dry-run ownership checks; unify atomic annotation accounting and exactly-once synchronization; reject ambiguous dependency owners; make durable file flushing Windows-compatible; reject backslash URL paths; align fresh/replayed privacy preflight; isolate closeout identity conflicts to eligible item rows. Preserve accepted ownership and all earlier regressions. Every fix gets behavioral revert evidence in disposable copies, real SDK controls and bounded affected-file gates. No review threads will be answered or resolved."
  "2026-11-12T01:42:41.626Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 7 decisions and implementation: dry-run needs an initialized real tracker so preview checks the same destination ownership as apply; atomic and plain preview fixtures now seed native SDK owners, remove fabricated pm reads/commit APIs, and assert item/history bytes and transaction-plan absence. Committed atomic imports return commentWriteFailures and annotationIssueNumbers, remove the plan despite best-effort comment refusals and let gated callers refuse incomplete side data through the shared divergence check. The outer loop handles only entries not already synchronized. Dependency indexing retains only unique explicit owners, excludes contradictory claims, and reports ambiguous_github_dependency_owner with all claimant IDs without linking. Both fresh gated and ungated atomic plans require passing privacy preflight before publication; legacy failed/missing/forged-plan regressions now seed a real interrupted clean journal before constructing legacy recovery inputs. GitHub path parsing rejects raw/encoded backslashes before WHATWG normalization while allowing query/fragment text. File fsync uses writable r+ handles; directory fsync is explicitly skipped on win32. The package-wide flush search found a second instance in webhook receipt recovery; it now uses the same helper. Tests stub only platform selection and keep filesystem operations real. Closeout catches identity and ownership conflicts as per-item outcomes and does not check explicitly skipped, context-only or foreign references; unrelated valid deliveries still close. Existing curated-reopen behavior remains deferred and no review thread was answered or resolved."
  "2026-11-12T01:42:43.636Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 7 behavioral revert receipt, disposable copies only: reverting commitGithubImportTransactionUnchecked causes 2 atomic annotation-failure regressions to fail while 2 plain controls pass; removing the outer annotation receipt skip causes 2 changed/mixed exactly-once failures while the unchanged control passes. Reverting buildProvenanceIndexFromMetadata causes both ambiguous source/target regressions to fail while the unique-owner control passes. Restoring the previous read-only file-sync policy causes all 3 platform regressions to fail; restoring unconditional directory sync causes the win32 case to fail and POSIX controls to pass. Reverting parseGithubUrl causes 3 backslash-normalization regressions to fail, with 2 previously rejected encodings plus must-allow query/trailing-slash controls retained. Reinstating gated-only fresh preflight causes the ungated regression to fail while the gated control passes. Reverting closeoutAttempt causes all 4 eligible/skipped/context/foreign scenarios to abort instead of closing the unrelated valid delivery. Restoring the original atomic dry-run fixture reproduces tracker_root_missing (1 failure); fixed fixtures use native SDK init/create/mutateItem. Restored focused tests pass 21/21. Commands use node --test --test-concurrency=1 with the Round7, durable-state, backslash and atomic dry-run name patterns; source/package production files were never reverted in the real worktree. Whole atomic.test.ts passed 11/11; broad bounded dependent sweep is underway with a maximum of 2 workers."
  "2026-11-12T02:01:16.029Z",codex-github230-1111,"Read the newest nonempty CodeRabbit review body in full (20 reviews enumerated, 34 threads / 42 comments, no further thread pages). The 10 additional observations beyond covered explicit-closeout and dry-run cases are consolidated, pending validation, in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/236 and pm-github-reference-identity-followup, following the instruction to use one follow-up instead of round 8. All 10 full comment bodies and AI-agent prompts were read. The dependency-index half of auB7 is already addressed; its blocker self-exclusion half stays in that follow-up. The review request to remove earlier accepted scope and mandatory tracker files is not applied: prior rounds are accepted and tracker history must remain append-only. No review thread was replied to or resolved. Three older annotation fixtures in coverage-remainder relied on fabricated pm snapshots/commit results and stopped at provenance validation; they now use real stored owners and a native SDK policy refusal, with explicit annotation-failure counts and committed-plan cleanup assertions. Final regression rechecks will cover those fixtures, direct atomic APIs, replay, real HTTP dry runs and all closeout eligibility exclusions."
  "2026-11-12T02:50:42.074Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 7 final self-review and test receipt: all 73 import-gate cases pass in four disjoint name partitions. The 57-file affected/required sweep has 60 bounded invocations; 56 completed files / 59 completed invocations contain 1290 tests: 1288 pass, zero remaining failures, two existing pm-cli#1656 skips. closeout-workflow reaches its 20-minute cap after 42 passes and one cancellation without an assertion failure; CI certifies that file and the full npm/Bun release/coverage gate. Final whole-file rechecks pass atomic 11/11, ownership 26/26, closeout 93/93, corrected coverage-remainder 25/25, and real HTTP dry-run preview 2/2. Linked pm runs of node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/round-seven.test.ts and bun test --timeout 60000 test/round-seven.test.ts pass 23/23 each; node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/durable-state.test.ts passes 3/3. Project policy disables automatic run artifacts, so results remain in comments. Bun exposed event coalescing in a filesystem-watcher assertion; the test now observes actual native SDK mutations, advancing only its incoming fixture cursor so an unwanted second pass would append an extra annotation. No pm API or filesystem is mocked. Unchanged and mixed entries have explicit controls. Extra tests cover committed-plan replay, direct gated atomic APIs, contradictory dependency identities, shared reference-only mentions, and all closeout exclusions including terminal items and epics. Production code was frozen before these final rechecks; additional observations are consolidated in issue #236."
  "2026-11-12T02:50:43.885Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 7 final behavioral revert evidence in disposable copies: reverting commitGithubImportTransactionUnchecked produces six atomic annotation/refusal failures with two plain controls passing; removing only the outer receipt skip produces two exactly-once failures with the unchanged control passing. Reverting the dependency index produces three failures (duplicate source, duplicate target, contradictory identity), while the unique owner plus reference-only mentions passes. Restoring read-only file flushing produces three platform failures; restoring unconditional directory flushing produces one win32 failure with POSIX controls passing. Reverting the URL parser produces three backslash normalization failures and retains two existing must-refuse controls. Restoring gated-only fresh privacy preflight produces one ungated failure while the gated control passes. Reverting closeoutAttempt produces six failures across eligible, explicit-skip, context, foreign, terminal and epic references, each with an unrelated valid delivery. Restoring the old atomic dry-run fixture produces tracker_root_missing (one failure). Restored focused tests pass 28/28. After replacing filesystem event counting, repeated the exactly-once revert against the final fixture: both changed/mixed cases fail and the unchanged control passes; restored focused tests again pass 28/28. Source commands are node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern PATTERN FILE with ^Round7 annotation refusal, ^Round7 atomic annotations, ^Round7 dependency, ^Round7 failed atomic preflight, ^Round7 closeout, ^GitHub ownership rejects backslash, ^atomic dry-run, plus test/durable-state.test.ts. No tracked implementation was reverted or native audit history rewritten. Main and base histories remain append-only. CI handoff: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233/checks . Releasing only this author claim; the main item stays in progress and the consolidated follow-up remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-11-12T06:13:06.006Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 8 starts from accepted head f252e3e; merged current main before implementation. Read the four blocking threads, the added ownership-preflight cleanup thread and outside-diff deletion-durability comment in review 5868419634 in full, including agent prompts. Scope is only shared ownership consistency/uniqueness at locked writes plus safe plan cleanup and the existing directory-flush policy. Other findings remain in issue #236 and no review thread will be answered or resolved. Asked for clarification of tag-only references versus the new claim rule; pending an answer, preserve the original requirement that reference-only items are not owners, while validating all claims on provenance-bearing items. Add one real SDK matrix across matching, closeout and replay, plus native concurrent-peer and cleanup/journal controls, then bounded affected-file gates and behavioral reverts."
  "2026-11-12T06:49:20.097Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 8: merged current main and read all five scoped review threads, including agent prompts and proposed changes, plus review 5868419634 outside-index-1745. Shared normalized claims now include external_ref, supported legacy link fields, explicit URL aliases, partial repository/number provenance and tags on provenance-bearing records. Reference-only tags remain non-owning, preserving the original import contract. Every native update checks current agreement and competing claims under the SDK lock; replay also checks persisted provenance before gated success. The 77-case real-tracker matrix passes, including 14 contradiction/ambiguity shapes across match, plain import, atomic import, closeout and gated replay, consistent legacy/full controls, late peer claims, no-journal cleanup, journal retention and native directory-flush failure. Scoped gates are running with two total workers and per-command 20-minute limits."
  "2026-11-12T07:20:14.799Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 8 compatibility note: the stricter claim rule intentionally changes earlier permissive cases where a provenance-bearing item referenced a different issue or repository. Those records now refuse with github_import_owner_conflict, keep their native item/history bytes and do not create a competing import. Reference-only records remain shareable. Updated the earlier round-two/three and reference regression expectations to match this extended contract. Plain creates and all owned mutations now use guarded native SDK writes; command-failure fixtures use real SDK policy refusals instead of child-CLI interception. The aggregate closeout workflow command reached its 20-minute cap after 49 passing cases and one canceled file wrapper; CI must certify its remaining workflow matrix."
  "2026-11-12T07:43:53.586Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 8 revert proof, using disposable source copies and real SDK trackers: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern \"^Ownership matrix (?:match|plain|atomic|closeout|replay): refuses\" test/ownership-consistency.test.ts fails 70/70 when the changed ownership functions are reverted, including matchImportedIssue and the closeout check. Reverting only uniqueness in assertGithubOwnershipConsistency makes all four \"^Ownership matrix locked\" cases fail. Reverting commitGithubImportTransaction plan cleanup makes \"^Ownership preflight removes\" fail 1/1. Reverting removeGithubImportPlan directory flushing makes \"^Recovery-plan deletion flushes\" fail 1/1. Restoring the implementation passes 82/82. The same 82-case matrix passed through pm test --run --only-index 74 --progress --timeout 1200; native policy-failure coverage passes 25/25. Removed the auxiliary PR tag from this issue-owned item so every identity claim agrees on issue 230; PR 233 remains a docs reference. Item/history and native state are never repaired or rewritten."
  "2026-11-12T07:47:10.726Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 8 final local evidence: 58 selected test files, using at most two total workers and a 1200-second command cap. Effective distinct outcomes after the documented reruns: 1422 reported tests, 1419 passed, zero assertion failures, two existing SDK-related skips, one canceled aggregate closeout-workflow wrapper at its 20-minute cap (49 workflow cases passed before cancellation). CI certifies the remaining workflow decision matrix and full release gates. The 82-case ownership matrix passes through pm on both Node and Bun; 76 refusal/durability assertions fail on their corresponding behavioral reverts (70 ownership shapes, four late claims, plan cleanup, directory flush), and restoration passes 82/82. Native policy-failure coverage passes 25/25. Build, test compilation, lint, typecheck, docstrings and duplication passed; 33 authored modules have zero duplicated lines. All 61 initial scoped command variants are already linked among the 75 item tests. Read the complete 38-thread snapshot, all five scoped threads with agent prompts, and the one scoped outside-diff comment. Deferred findings remain in issue 236; no review replies or resolutions were made. The ownership corpus read can create derived SDK caches, so fresh atomic privacy preflight now runs before that read; the real-tracker fresh/replayed privacy regressions pass 29/29. Existing audit histories remain append-only. Exact-head CI evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233/checks ."
  "2026-11-12T08:41:04.182Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 9 resumes from bd8d52d with a clean worktree. Current main is already merged. Read the three blocking CodeRabbit threads and agent prompts: follow-up reference tag, durable creation proof, and SDK 2026.10.17 compilation. Scope stays limited to those findings; the three non-blocking observations remain in issue 236. Plan: replace stray PR tags with docs references across changed tracker records, separate creation provenance from item naming and issue ownership, and retain revision fencing through a typed minimum-SDK fallback. Run the four scoped real-tracker suites plus current/floor typecheck, lint and changelog checks under 20-minute command limits."
  "2026-11-12T08:59:05.505Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 9: the 90-case matrix passes. Audited all seven tracker records added or changed by this PR; moved six contextual parent issue/PR tags to docs links, retaining only matching issue-230 and issue-236 identity tags. Creation proof now uses package author or an explicit github_import boolean, never an ID. New creates record pm-github as creator, and locked writes refuse an original mirroring plan if its target loses creation proof. Unknown-origin legacy records keep identity compatibility but preserve curated content. The isolated minimum-SDK job found both the GetResult.item_hash field and PmClient.withExpectedItemRevisions method unavailable at SDK 2026.10.17. Replaced them with native document/hash reads and a locked revision check using APIs available at that floor. The packed consumer now compiles all production/operational sources and declarations, exercises an owned update, and refuses a stale revision at SDK 2026.10.17. No SDK floor or dependency pins were raised. Scoped suite reruns retain the existing diagnostics for curated collisions and missing items."
  "2026-11-12T09:15:18.711Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 9 revert proof in disposable copies: adding the former PR-233 tag back through the SDK makes the PR tracker audit fail 1/1; removing it restores 1/1. Reverting only importerCreatedItem to its ID-suffix implementation makes all seven Creation proof tests fail: two curated-ID cases, four provenance-backed non-pattern-ID controls, and a stale mirroring-plan refusal. Restoring it passes 7/7. Restoring the previous readGithubImportOwner and mutateGithubOwnedItem makes timeout 1200 npm run test:minimum-sdk fail with TS2339 for both GetResult.item_hash and PmClient.withExpectedItemRevisions at SDK 2026.10.17; restoring the native document/hash and locked revision guard passes the same floor job. Final restored matrix: 90/90. The data revert and restoration used native append-only SDK mutations; no existing history record was rewritten."
  "2026-11-12T09:15:19.533Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 9 final local gates: ownership-consistency 90/90 on Node and Bun through pm; import-ownership 26/26; import-fidelity 53 passed plus one existing pm-cli#1656 skip; closeout 93/93. Four-file total: 263 reported, 262 passed, one existing skip, no failures or cancellations. timeout 1200 npm run test:minimum-sdk passes 1/1 through pm against exact SDK 2026.10.17, including all authored source/declaration typechecks, a guarded owned update and stale-revision refusal. Current build, test compilation, lint and typecheck pass; docstrings, zero duplication and privacy checks pass. All test commands stayed below 20 minutes with at most two workers. Read 45 complete thread inventory entries and the full three scoped blocking threads with their agent prompts. No thread replies or resolutions were made. All seven PR tracker records were audited; six contextual references became docs links, while the matching issue-230/236 tags remain. The other three findings stay deferred to issue 236. Exact-head release certification remains CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233/checks ."
  "2026-11-12T10:01:49.068Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 10 starts from d9d9bc7 with a clean worktree; fetched main is already merged. Read the complete named codex verdict and issue 236. Inventory first: added docs/identity-ownership-inventory.md with every ownership-helper call and direct identity-field access grouped by enclosing function. Confirmed bypasses in upstreamTargets and dependency indexing; the audit also identifies refresh, Projects issue association, search association, diagnostics, blocker self-exclusion, and remote execution rechecks. Route target selectors through shared claims while documenting explicit-source and reference-only operations that do not select owned targets. Tests will use real SDK trackers and HTTP transport, including consistent controls and revert proofs."
  "2026-11-12T10:16:18.201Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 10 inventory identified direct selectors in outbound sync/export, dependency indexing, refresh, search, Projects issue association and blocker self-exclusion. Operational selectors now share ownership claims and consistency/uniqueness checks. Dependency endpoints are checked again inside the native source mutation lock; outbound writes re-read current tracker ownership. The initial 47 outbound/dependency SDK and real-HTTP regressions pass. Broad importer-consumer checks are running with two workers and a 20-minute per-file limit."
  "2026-11-12T10:46:00.601Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 10 ownership matrix passes 161/161 through pm test (one selected command, source workspace; project policy keeps test-result tracking disabled). The completed source inventory has 83 function groups and 248 helper/field/parser sites, plus five script/workflow text matches reviewed with no independent owner selector. Direct importIdentityKeys consumption is now restricted to the shared claims implementation. Shared URL-kind and direct-provenance facets preserve native declaration lifecycle classification and exclude legacy PR links from issue refresh. Search, Projects issue association, blocker self-exclusion and sync hints also use shared claims; unrelated reference parsing, labels, board IDs and explicit source arguments are documented as non-owning. Real-tracker label-model and literal-assignment compatibility fixtures now declare importer provenance instead of relying on naming. Disposable behavioral reverts and remaining bounded consumer gates are running."
  "2026-11-12T10:49:29.639Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 10 behavioral revert proof in a disposable source copy: restoring the complete index.ts from d9d9bc7 makes every selected new case fail: 34/34 ^Outbound ownership, 13/13 ^Dependency ownership, 16/16 ^Ownership routing inventory:, and 2/2 ^Ownership sync hint. Restoring only selectRefreshTargets from that head makes 1/1 ^Refresh ownership kind: fail. Commands use node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern PATTERN test/ownership-consistency.test.ts, each capped at 1200 seconds. Every failure is an assertion/observable diagnostic or missing-refusal failure, with zero import/syntax setup failures and zero cancellations. Restoring all fixed source files makes the combined 66/66 cases pass. The package worktree was never reverted; native tracker storage and the real HTTP transport/server are used. The exact partial github_repo-versus-URL reproduction sends no HTTP writes with the fix."
  "2026-11-12T11:01:33.165Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 10 final bounded gate evidence: 52 unique test files, 1439 cases, 1437 pass, 0 fail, 2 existing pm-cli#1656 quarantines, 0 cancellations. All 48 direct consumers of changed modules were read and tested, plus three additional closeout files and the minimum-SDK consumer. Commands are timeout 1200 node --test --test-concurrency=1 TEST_FILE, with at most two total workers. Ownership matrix: 161/161 through pm test. Link-deps: 28/28; import-ownership: 26/26; import-fidelity: 53 pass plus one existing skip; refresh: 34 pass plus one existing skip; closeout core/attribution/revision/selection: 93/12/110/82 passes; Projects: 39/39 and integration 19/19; packed npm/native Bun projection: 6/6. The full import-gate file completed 73 cases within its 20-minute cap; its two old diagnostic assertions were updated and rerun by exact names, yielding 73/73 final case evidence. Fixture corrections retain curated safety and explicitly mark genuine importer mirrors. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint and npm run docstring pass. npm run test:minimum-sdk passes its exact 2026.10.17 packed consumer (all production/operational modules, declarations, owned write and stale revision refusal); no dependency or engine floor changed. Privacy scanned 8749 existing objects with approved identities and no secret/host-path findings. Changelog is regenerated after this final tracker write and claim release. Full npm/Bun release and exact 100-percent coverage remain for CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233/checks . The priority external_ref dependency ambiguity in issue 236 is fixed here; other deferred observations remain there. Two supplied codex review findings were read in full; no review threads were replied to or resolved. Releasing only this author claim and leaving the item in_progress."
  "2026-11-12T11:17:18.992Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 11: reread issue 230 Expected and revert-test contract, plus all five scoped review threads and AI-agent prompts. The round-8 tag-claim rule is replaced: plain gh reference tags never confer ownership or conflicts, including on linked items. Preserve explicit provenance conflicts and legacy importer-created IDs with their verified repository hash. Build ownership indexes once per snapshot, share pre-journal corpus reads and transaction-local locked reads, and retain fresh outbound checks. Add real SDK regressions and deterministic N=40 cost counts; align URL mention normalization and complete preview byte snapshots. Public scratch-clone previews are read-only, capped at 15 minutes and about 60 API calls, with cleanup. Main has not moved from the existing merged ancestor."
  "2026-11-12T11:47:48.604Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 11 contract: plain gh: tags are mentions on every item and never promoted, constrained or enabled by the deprecated upstream flag. Proven importer IDs use the shared repository hash plus creation provenance, preserving legacy records without github_number. Ownership snapshots now index claims once, batch native preflight reads peers once and locked checks reuse one snapshot; outbound writes read one fresh corpus and validate only the current target. Added native N=40 work-count regressions, API mention grouping, full byte-snapshot controls and tag/legacy compatibility cases. Public preview completed with unchanged clone bytes and zero legacy duplicates; detailed counts and privacy refusals will be recorded after final validation."
  "2026-11-12T11:51:05.856Z",codex-github230-1111,"Read-only public-check discrepancy: pm-context and pm-linear proposals have zero legacy-ID duplicates and no curated-field replacements, but their existing GitHub bodies trigger batch privacy refusals (two and five findings respectively). pm-review has no privacy/ownership refusal and no title replacements; its proven pm-github-authored importer record for issue 14 would restore source created_at, consistent with the accepted mirroring rule but different from the brief expectation that all four referenced records are curated. The other three retain curated timestamps. No clone was committed, pushed or left behind; completed checks preserve file bytes. We will report this exception explicitly rather than change importer mirroring to hide it."
  "2026-11-12T11:57:30.922Z",codex-github230-1111,"Final-build public previews reused cached public REST/timeline payloads without additional API calls: pm-context 221 creates / 3 matching updates / one batch privacy refusal; pm-linear 217 / 1 / one batch privacy refusal; pm-review 82 / 1 / zero refusals. Zero ownership refusals, zero legacy duplicates and no curated-field replacement in all three. pm-linear-toolchain-1104 stays untouched. The four named review records keep their titles; the proven importer-authored issue-14 record would restore its source created_at, while the three curated records keep theirs. All three clone byte snapshots match and all clones were deleted. Total public calls: 59; active read-only checks stayed under 15 minutes. The early attempt that did not preserve clone bytes was discarded and rerun with read-only clones and optional Git index refresh disabled; only the completed byte-identical previews support these results."
  "2026-11-12T12:02:45.295Z",codex-github230-1111,"Self-review of the inventory found an old closeout suffix-only destination fence beside the new shared helper. Removed that independent identity check: only a repository-hash-verified importer ID constrains ownership; a naming pattern for an unrelated repository cannot contradict otherwise consistent explicit provenance. Added a real-SDK closeout must-allow control and scoped legacy-ID resolution to the known delivery/project/dependency repositories. Creation proof still requires importer author or github_import metadata, and genuine explicit/ID conflicts remain refused. The native cost test now also exercises nested metadata finalizers inside its actual SDK transaction."
  "2026-11-12T12:32:44.275Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 11 core gates: ownership-consistency 142/142; reference-import-identity 17/17; N=40 native batch including nested finalizers uses exactly two corpus reads and 360 claim parses; outbound 40-item sync uses 1640 claim parses, preserving fresh per-write checks. The first import-gate command reached its 1200-second cap after 64 passes and one runner cancellation; the nine uncompleted workflow cases are scheduled separately. All scoped threads and AI-agent prompts were read in full (five threads); the deferred durable-reader observation stays in issue 236. No review threads were replied to or resolved. The routing ledger has 88 function groups and 259 helper-call/field/parser sites."
  "2026-11-12T12:44:41.254Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 11 behavioral revert proof, entirely in a disposable package copy: restoring tag-as-owner claims fails 5/5 Reference contract cases and all 6/6 issue-230 Chore/shared-reference/mirror cases. Disabling verified importer-ID ownership fails 1/1 legacy resync case. Restoring the prior native ownership wrapper fails 1/1 N=40 work bound; restoring prior upstream target rebuilding fails 1/1 outbound bound. Restoring the old closeout suffix fence fails 1/1 hash control, the old API mention key fails 1/1 grouping case, and the old preview file filter fails 2/2 byte-snapshot cases. Total: 18 expected assertion failures across eight groups, zero setup/import errors or cancellations. Restoring the fix passes 17/17 combined controls plus 6/6 issue-230 cases. Commands: timeout 1200 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern PATTERN TEST_FILE, using ownership-consistency.test.ts or reference-import-identity.test.ts. The package worktree was never reverted. The complete 142-case matrix also passed through pm test --run --only-index 77 --progress; npm run test:minimum-sdk passed the exact 2026.10.17 packed consumer."
  "2026-11-12T12:50:46.076Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 11 final bounded evidence: all 51 direct/dependent test files plus the minimum-SDK consumer were read and exercised. Final case evidence across 52 unique files: 1420 tests, 1418 pass, zero remaining failures/cancellations, two unchanged pm-cli#1656 SDK quarantines (import-fidelity and refresh). The first import-gate attempt capped at 1200 seconds after 64 passes; all nine remaining cases passed separately, giving 73/73 distinct workflow cases. Final-source closeout core/attribution/revision/selection pass 93/12/110/82; Projects integration 19/19; importer ownership 26/26; reference identity 17/17; matrix 142/142 through pm test. Corrected legacy tag/declaration fixtures use explicit links or proven importer creation, and curated no-op fixtures assert retained local dates. Every command used at most two total test workers and a 1200-second cap. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run lint and npm run docstring pass (301 documented declarations). npm run test:minimum-sdk passes the exact declared 2026.10.17 packed consumer. Privacy audited 8787 existing Git objects with approved identities and no secret/host-path matches. Behavioral proof remains 18/18 failures on eight reverts and 23/23 after restoration. Public preview totals remain 59 API calls, zero legacy duplicates/ownership refusals and unchanged clone bytes; pm-context and pm-linear have existing-source privacy refusals, while the proven importer-created pm-review issue-14 record would restore source created_at. No public tracker or hold was changed. All seven listed per-repository reference-tag cleanup workarounds are unnecessary under this rule. The deferred reader thread stays in issue 236. Releasing only this claim; this item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification. Full release, coverage, npm/Bun and exact-head CI certification remain at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233/checks . Changelog is regenerated after this final tracker write and release."
